Use 60 KiB DOS COPY requests for regular-file writes to the physical USB
floppy. Resolve the opened target handle rather than parsing a drive letter,
so relative paths and concatenation use the same policy. Devices and other
DOS drives retain 32 KiB requests. USB command sizes and per-write commits
remain controlled by the transport.

--- a/src/shell/shell_cmds.cpp
+++ b/src/shell/shell_cmds.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 #include "build_timestamp.h"
 #include "version_string.h"
 #include "pi_dos_version.h"
+#include "pidos_usb_floppy_api.h"
 
 #include <output/output_ttf.h>
 
